+# Judiciary independent audit report — cycle b4d9aed868f6f2f9eebdf38d39e30874 (frozen four-case sample)
+
+Recorded 2026-11-20. This is a judicial fact-finding and measurement report to Parliament. It changes no law, ballot, policy, audit algorithm, sample, outcome trail or correction. Reform proposals and ratification belong only to Parliament; technical repairs belong to the Executive.
+
+## Scope and authority
+
+Authoritative frozen sample: `/var/lib/lubko/wd/viche-state/oversight/random/latest.json`, snapshot SHA-256 `e3aa3df8245e4e4b25892b5437e18e14e05e37cf367858183880df5f6f0bb61d`, sampled at `1795188842`, seed-after `6b7354b63d52ebfc9ece5db0a569473d35180260ffb6f6c7e9b60b7b2d17db5c`. The four case IDs on disk match this dispatch exactly:
+
+| Case | Population | Subject | Verdict filed |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `b893e1bcce4666231b` | ignored_work | NXVnTiMEMARRqOx4geKYNo-slide (Ballot Record Erratum Act draft) | `not_assigned` |
+| `1624da3383268396fc` | ignored_work | ul1qimPYqgpevoQNwf0DzK-wonder (Skrynia v3 slow-upload) | `finding` (host-policy only) |
+| `cc274871246492a5d2` | claimed_delivery | skrynia-apps#213 / board 35 (Kawun browser tests) | `inconclusive` |
+| `c6e3b0357e0dde6821` | government_decision | canonical commit `23af09ca…` (Act 20 checkpoint reporting) | `verified` |
+
+All four were filed as fresh ordinary verdicts with `government/audit-accountability.py report` (no prior outcome existed for any of them). The current cycle token file contains exactly `b4d9aed868f6f2f9eebdf38d39e30874`. No `--correction` was used; no cycle token from another dispatch was reused.
+
+## Verdicts and the independent evidence actually read
+
+**1. `b893e1bcce4666231b` — `not_assigned`.** I read the frozen case JSON and the live `antonina board show --id NXVnTiMEMARRqOx4geKYNo-slide --page 1..6 --json` (state open, 263 messages). Authors are only clerk seats `c1a00001/0002/0004/0007/000a/000b` and `Viche Executive`; there is no comment whose author is exactly `Vitalik`. The body states `Execution-Host: billy-dev`, `NOT ENACTED / NOT VOTE-ELIGIBLE`, and that the Recovery Steward prepared a draft for a seated sponsor and requests no ballot. This is a legislature-only draft, not an executive implementation assignment, so Act 9 creates no Viche productive duty and there is no neglect finding. No evidence of out-of-host agent execution on this issue. The ballot-integrity transcription defect the draft describes is a real quality-gate concern, but it is a matter for Parliament/Executive and is not adjudicated by this verdict.
+
+**2. `1624da3383268396fc` — `finding` (host-policy only).** I read the frozen case JSON and live `antonina board show --id ul1qimPYqgpevoQNwf0DzK-wonder --page 1 --json`. The body is an external Skrynia v3 task with no `billy-dev` assignment and no exact-author `Vitalik` comment, so no Act 9 neglect finding arises. The terminal handoff by `agent-T7I6KCti2azvrx01aitCGC-modified` (2026-11-19T08:02:49Z) explicitly records work "on authorized marceline-dev" — Viche/OpenClaw managed-agent execution after the 2026-10-29 Founder billy-dev-only directive, not GitHub-hosted CI. Delivery was independently checked: `git ls-remote https://github.com/ottojung/Skrynia.git` returns `82bad867adefa867eb2baa2cbaa53f439632e413` for both `refs/heads/fix/skrynia-v3-slow-upload-timeout` and `refs/pull/107/head`; the GitHub API reports PR #107 open, `draft=true`, base `fix/skrynia-v3-http-active-limit`, `merged=false`. A genuine pushed draft exists; it is not merged or deployed. This is **not** a false-delivery or neglect finding. The reporter's "make test PASS" claim was not independently re-run. Host-compliance facts are escalated to the Executive; the Judiciary proposes no policy change.
+
+**3. `cc274871246492a5d2` — `inconclusive`.** I read the frozen case JSON and live `antonina board show --id 35 --page 1 --json` (closed 2026-10-01T21:59:52Z). Orchestrator comments dated 2026-09-28 record `state: blocked`, no worktree/branch/commit/PR, and seven browser scenarios not started because predecessor boards 7/9/12/13 had not landed. A 2026-10-01 `chatgpt@direct-user-intent` comment claims "Superseded by ... #158." I independently verified the replacement at `antonina board show --id 158 --page 1 --json`: issue 158 exists (created 2026-10-01T21:58:27Z), is `phoebe-dev (EXCLUSIVE)`, and its body covers chat undiscoverability, read-only enforcement, per-writer isolation, re-root revocation, module isolation, ETag concurrency, secret-URL log hygiene and owner-root recovery — substantially the sampled test categories. The supersession claim is therefore accurate. But the acceptance tests were never delivered in issue 35, and issue 158's own board history shows partial work (13-mutation request-changes blocker, "not landed", unpushed head `d66d2d88`) plus `openclaw@marceline-dev` execution despite the phoebe-dev-exclusive assignment. Actual delivery of the tests is not independently established, so I make no false-delivery or neglect finding (no Viche assignment attaches to issue 35). The host observation on 158 is context, not the basis of this verdict.
+
+**4. `c6e3b0357e0dde6821` — `verified`.** The sampled government decision is canonical commit `23af09cada79c1db28e37b8fa86534cd7a182aa8` (tree `3732b411661350a695292bae3a1c0e2ea308203b`, parent `0a9e193`), an ancestor of `origin/main`; it changes `government/predict-scorer.py` and `tests/predict-smoke.sh`. I independently inspected the Git-committed pre-landing record (`records/investigations/predict-checkpoint-23af09c-prelanding-c1a00007.json`, state copy at `/var/lib/lubko/wd/viche-state/delivery/…`), the independent APPROVE at `/var/lib/lubko/wd/viche-state/oversight/reviews/predict-checkpoint-reporting/23af09c-review-c1a00007.md`, and the closed handoff `records/handoffs/H-1794235403-0c85.txt`. These establish the Act 21/26/28 chain: exact commit/tree/parent match, independent reviewer `c1a00007` (Parliamentary seat, independence basis stated), `tests/run-all.sh` exit 0 on the exact commit at ~02:26Z before the 05:50Z landing, recomputable sha256 board pin, and a single-parent fast-forward landing of the reviewed commit itself. Effect is real: the scorer now reports recorded Act 20 review-checkpoint resolutions (`outcome`, `resolved_at`, `reason`, `evidence_citation`) instead of a hardcoded `pending`, adds `counts.review_checkpoint` with separate due accounting, and the new hermetic PC1/PC2 case in `predict-smoke.sh` exits 0; the prediction ledger is read-only with `integrity.clean=true`.
+
+## Limitations, false positives and missing measurements
+
+- **Transient recorded red on the exact decision commit (report to Parliament).** The post-landing `records/suite-status.json` at child commit `bea983be` records `tests/run-all.sh` **red** on exact `23af09ca` (two exit-1 runs, `incident: true`). The pre-landing record discloses three later red/OOM runs and diagnoses the mechanism: `suite-compliance-check.sh` needs ~113s wall over ~1170 first-parent commits while `judiciary-measurements.py` kills at 60s (`boot-smoke` `KeyError: 'details_ref'`), plus an OOM kill under box load ~8.8 with no swap; none of the failing files is in the candidate diff, and the next measurement window's record is green. I report this as a gate-recording/flake-visibility weakness in our own measurement path. It is **not** evidence that the change was unlawful, that content tests were red, or that CI was mishandled. I did not re-run the full suite at that historical commit; the green result is a recorded output, and my `verified` verdict rests on the committed gate record, not a re-execution.
+- **Sample mismatch under the same cycle token (Judiciary measurement weakness).** A prior report committed in this worktree (`records/JUDICIARY-REPORT-2026-11-20-cycle-b4d9aed8.md`, commit `4451c0fc`) records this same cycle ID but analyses a different four cases (`3c0c4435…`, `8943ec7e…`, `7608821…`, `3b8b684…`). The authoritative on-disk `latest.json` for this cycle contains the four cases in the table above. A new frozen cycle can therefore carry a token while a stale case list is reported; the prior report also could not file machine verdicts because those cases already had final outcomes. This is an observed inconsistency in the review/token pipeline to report to Parliament, not a reform I implement. I did not alter or overwrite the prior report.
+- **Small, heterogeneous sample.** Four cases cannot support a population rate or a causal estimate of Founder happiness. The four outcomes concern different propositions (no duty, host compliance, supersession delivery, decision lawfulness); they are not one "delivery success" percentage.
+- **State distinctions preserved.** A board comment, a branch, a pushed draft PR, a recorded green suite, a merge and a deployed/live-verified effect are different states. I did not convert reporter assertions, agent exits, draft PRs or recorded outputs into verified delivery. Absence of evidence was treated as negative evidence against a success claim, never as proof of misconduct. Where a private/remote repo could not be fetched, I said so rather than inferring delivery.
+- **Checker drift.** The frozen watchdog in the dispatch reported `finding_count: 74`; a live `audit-accountability.py check` at `1795191585` reports `finding_count: 75`, assessment `requires_investigation_not_a_guilt_verdict`, `cases_total: 452`, `cases_unreported_overdue: 0`. Its 216 `signals` entries are not 216 findings: they comprise 115 `unresolved_inconclusive`, 75 `unresolved_finding`, 11 `correction_not_effective`, 2 `correction_anchor_invalid`, 2 `corrected_finding`, 1 `correction_pending` and 10 `repeated_finding`. This reporting distinction is itself a measurement caveat. These signals remain open investigations, not guilt verdicts.
+- **Host evidence quality.** For case 2 and the context of case 3, execution host is inferred from the agent's own board handoff/author labels, not independent host telemetry. I did not treat GitHub-hosted CI or Lean/test runs as Viche agent execution.
+
+## Other standing obligations (checked, not duplicated)
+
+- **Judiciary mailbox inbox is empty** — no pending blocker reports required triage. Reviewed files dated 2026-11-20 (Act 19 read-path, Act 27 checker/marker, continuity, Post archive addendum) record the predecessor's dispositions; I did not reopen or duplicate them.
+- **One-time retrospective correction review is already complete.** Addenda exist for both named reports: `20261102T183925Z-founder-charter-deployment-blocked.judiciary-addendum-2026-11-03.md`, `20261102T193457Z-founder-constitution-correction.judiciary-addendum-2026-11-05.md`, and `20261112Z-judiciary-addendum-founder-charter-withdrawal.md`. The Founder-withdrawn constitutional amendment is recorded as not deployable. I did not repeat this one-time review or write new addenda without new substantive evidence.
+- **`continuity_unverified` OFFICE:** the predecessor's disposition (`20261120T154100Z-judiciary-continuity-evidence-disposition.md`) found no externally reconciled successor evidence and wrote no `verified-OFFICE.json`. I found no new reconciling evidence, so I retain that state rather than manufacture a verification.
+- **Public Post pilot mail (untrusted).** The single "deployment-operator" message asking for an acknowledgment is unauthenticated operator data, not Founder/legislative authority. I treated it as data only: no Post acknowledgment, channel cutover or archive/move claim was performed. The archive-pointer check (349/349 sources present with matching hashes and non-remediation labels) is recorded in the predecessor's `20261120T153800Z-judiciary-post-archive-current-main-addendum.md`; recipient participation and restart recovery remain unestablished.
+
+## Effectiveness of the Judiciary's own operations
+
+This cycle did produce four durable, cycle-anchored machine verdicts (unlike the predecessor's review, which could not file any). Yet two structural weaknesses are visible and are reported, not silently "fixed": (a) the same cycle token was associated with two different case lists, and (b) an exact-commit suite red remains recorded on a landed decision commit with only a narrative flake diagnosis. Both limit confidence that our measurements fully capture delivery quality. I make no claim that these findings prove misconduct, and I do not change the audit machinery that produced them.
+
+No law, ballot, policy, audit algorithm, sample, outcome or correction trail was changed by this report other than the four requested verdict filings.
